Package: threadfin
Type: Package
Title: R Interface to 'Threadfin' for Clone-Level Single-Cell Analysis
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Chen", "Satoshi", , "103236530+Reynold4k@users.noreply.github.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: An interface to the 'Python' package 'Threadfin'
    <https://github.com/Reynold4k/Threadfin> for paired single-cell RNA and
    B-cell or T-cell receptor (BCR or TCR) sequencing. Each clone is
    described by the distribution of its cells' transcriptional states, so
    that clones, not cells, are compared, mapped and tested: whether cells of
    one clone share their state, a map with one point per clone, groups of
    clones that behave alike, clone-level tests of measured labels, whether
    clones keep their state over time, and how far a clone's output lags
    behind its own germinal-centre cells. It takes 'h5ad' files, 'Seurat'
    and 'SingleCellExperiment' objects with Cell Ranger or AIRR receptor
    tables, and returns the results as data frames. Every analysis runs in
    'Threadfin' through 'reticulate', so results equal those of the 'Python'
    package.
